{
 "name": "nordic-eastern-europe",
 "note": "Poland, Czechia, Hungary, Russia, Ukraine, Belarus, Finland, Estonia and the Nordic countries, mostly through 'Paintings by <painter>' categories of artists who died before 1955 (taken whatever the file date), plus Russian and Ukrainian icons and the 'Paintings from <country>' categories. Categories and sizes checked on the Commons API 2026-10-28; the plain-name Repin, Polenov, Perov, Kramskoi, Mucha, Munkacsy (plain) categories are empty or missing so the 'Paintings by' names were used. IMPORTANT: most of these painters are already in the corpus through the museum batches (Google Art Project etc.), so expect the dedupe to drop a large share; the 'candidate' count of --status counts only new files. Slovakia, Latvia, Lithuania, Slovenia are in balkans-baltic. Left out as post-1955: Kupka (d.1957), Svabinsky (d.1962), Chagall, Malevich/Kandinsky are not painters of this list (Kandinsky d.1944 and Malevich d.1935 could be added later), Edvard Munch main (d.1944, very large, probably already in the corpus; Paintings by Edvard Munch has only 9 files).",
 "depth": 2,
 "date": {
  "from": 700,
  "to": 1925
 },
 "caps": {
  "per_group": 40,
  "total": 2500,
  "overshoot": 1.3
 },
 "skip_cat": "Calligraphy|Icon frames|Iconostasis|Church architecture|Posters|Postcards|Lubok|Banknotes",
 "filter": {
  "enabled": true,
  "text": 0.75,
  "blank": 0.5,
  "sketch": 0.5,
  "ornament": 0.6,
  "dup": 0.975,
  "text_prompt": "a page that is mostly lines of handwritten text"
 },
